*! test_option_surface.cscript
*! Certification script for the dash twoway OPTION SURFACE conformance claim.
*!
*! Plan task 05-02 (batch 2).  Every check in this file is a FAILING test
*! written BEFORE the fix, per project rule 8.  Each documents a defect that
*! was measured end to end against the pre-fix code base by plan task 05-01.
*!
*! ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*! WHAT IS BEING CERTIFIED
*! ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*! dash.sthlp:668-673 claims:
*!
*!     "No error is produced for unknown options, so existing Stata graph
*!      commands copy-pasted into dash will still run even when they contain
*!      options that have no Bokeh equivalent."
*!
*! That claim is false today.  dash's two -syntax- blocks (dash.ado:230 and
*! dash.ado:293) are closed allow-lists invoked with no -capture- and no
*! catch-all, so an unlisted option aborts the caller's do-file with r(198).
*! Task 05-01 measured 299 legal -twoway- commands through dash: 143 of them
*! abort, covering 115 distinct option keys plus 3 syntax constructs.
*!
*! THE CORE ASSERTION (O2-01) is therefore one line long: every command in
*! test/fixtures/twoway_corpus.do must return _rc == 0 from dash.  That single
*! assertion is what makes dash.sthlp:668-673 true.
*!
*! ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*! THE REPORTING CONTRACT
*! ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*! Accepting an option silently is not enough: a user whose title() or
*! kdensity bandwidth vanished must be able to see that it vanished.  The
*! decision taken for this project is:
*!
*!   an unsupported option is ACCEPTED, never aborts, and is reported in
*!   exactly ONE note per command that names EVERY unsupported option that
*!   command used.
*!
*! Concretely, the note is a single line of output of the form
*!
*!     dash: unsupported option(s) ignored: nodraw, play(), xoverhangs
*!
*! and the checks below require, for each command:
*!
*!   (a) exactly ONE output line containing the phrase "unsupported option"
*!       (matched case-insensitively; wrapped log continuations are re-joined
*!        before matching, so the phrasing around it is free);
*!   (b) that line names EVERY unsupported option the command used, each as a
*!       whole word (so "play" must appear as play, not merely inside
*!       "display");
*!   (c) it names NOTHING the command did not drop -- a supported option used
*!       in the same command must not be listed;
*!   (d) a command that uses no unsupported option emits NO such line at all.
*!
*! ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*! TESTS
*! ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*!   O2-01  HEADLINE   every command in the corpus fixture returns _rc == 0.
*!                     (today: 143 of 299 abort -- 115 option keys + 3
*!                      syntax constructs.)
*!   O2-02             every ZERO-OPTION command in the corpus emits NO note.
*!                     (the "no unsupported options => no note" half of the
*!                      contract, driven off the corpus controls.)
*!   O2-03             every option the fixture disposes as "accept-and-report"
*!                     is accepted (_rc == 0) and reported in one note that
*!                     names it.  Today that set is {nodraw, play, xoverhangs,
*!                     yoverhangs} and every one of them is r(198).
*!                     dash.sthlp:157-160 already promises a warning for
*!                     play() and nodraw; the promise is unimplemented.
*!   O2-04             all of those options in ONE command produce exactly ONE
*!                     note naming ALL of them -- and not naming the supported
*!                     option used alongside them.
*!   O2-05             a genuinely unknown option (notarealoption(3)) is
*!                     accepted and reported.
*!   O2-06             unsupported options spread across TWO plot segments are
*!                     BOTH reported, in that one note.
*!   O2-07             a command whose options are all supported emits NO note.
*!   O2-08             link() and filter() written on a graph belong to
*!                     dash build; twoway refuses both, r(198), and so
*!                     does dash (WP-32).
*!   O2-09             saving() on a NAMED graph is named once and writes
*!                     nothing (dash build writes a named graph).
*!   O2-10             the immediate render still honours saving() and is
*!                     not told otherwise.
*!   AC-13.1           a weight on a GLYPH layer is accepted and named
*!                     nowhere: the marker types size their markers by it
*!                     and the markerless types draw nothing different, as
*!                     twoway does (WP-31 C9; flipped from the WP-13 note
*!                     that named it by type).
*!
*! ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*! MEASURED STATUS WHEN THIS FILE WAS WRITTEN (pre-fix, branch
*! feature/batch2-syntax-surface)
*! ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*!   O2-01  FAIL   143 of 299 corpus commands abort.  The failing set is
*!                 identical, id for id and rc for rc, to the set recorded in
*!                 test/fixtures/rejected_options.json by task 05-01.
*!   O2-02  PASS   43 zero-option commands, 0 notes.  It passes vacuously
*!                 today because no note mechanism exists at all; it is here
*!                 as the guard against a "fix" that reports everything.
*!   O2-03  FAIL   4 of 4 -- nodraw, play(), xoverhangs, yoverhangs are all
*!                 r(198), although dash.sthlp:157-160 promises a warning for
*!                 the first two.
*!   O2-04  FAIL   r(198).
*!   O2-05  FAIL   r(198) on afcolor(red).
*!   O2-06  FAIL   r(198) on the two-segment command.
*!   O2-07  PASS   vacuously, as O2-02.
*!
*! The note-detection machinery itself (the wrapped-line re-join, the
*! one-note-exactly count, the whole-word option match) was verified against a
*! stub that DOES emit the note, so O2-02 and O2-07 are not passing because
*! the scanner is blind, and O2-03 to O2-06 will not pass on a note that fails
*! to name its options.
*!
*! ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*! FIXTURE-DRIVEN BY DESIGN
*! ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*! Nothing here hardcodes the corpus command list or the unsupported-option
*! list.  O2-01 and O2-02 parse test/fixtures/twoway_corpus.do directly, by
*! handing each -dashprobe- / -dashonlyprobe- line's arguments to a program
*! with the same -args- signature the corpus harness uses, so tokenisation is
*! identical.  O2-03 and O2-04 read the "accept-and-report" disposition out of
*! test/fixtures/rejected_options.json.  Adding probes to the corpus therefore
*! extends this test without editing it.
*!
*! The corpus's own data-fixture lines (sysuse auto / the synthetic tsset
*! panel) are replayed from the same file, so the t* probes see a tsset
*! dataset exactly as they did when task 05-01 measured them.  Only a
*! whitelist of data commands is replayed; the corpus's -program define-
*! blocks, -file- handles and probe by-products are never executed, so this
*! script writes nothing into the repository.
*!
*! Unlike most cscripts this one does NOT stop at the first failure: every
*! check is tallied so a single run reports the full state of the surface.
*! The script exits 9 if anything failed.
*!
*! Usage:  do test/test_option_surface.cscript
*! Version: 1.0

cscript "dash twoway option surface conformance" adodir ".."

// `cscript' drops every global macro, the runner's $dash_nobrowser with them;
// set it again before this script builds a dashboard (test_cscript_hygiene.py).
global dash_nobrowser 1

// Certification scripts share one Stata session, so start from a clean
// state: leftover data, globals, tsset settings or loaded programs from an
// earlier script otherwise leak in and change what this one measures.
clear all
// Certification timing: run_all_cscripts.do reads timer 100 when this
// script ends; with DASH_CERT_PROFILE set it also prints the profile.
timer clear 100
timer on 100
local _cert_prof : environment DASH_CERT_PROFILE
if "`_cert_prof'" != "" {
    capture profiler clear
    profiler on
}

// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// Dependency guards
// ----------------------------------------------------------------

// Do NOT probe with `capture python: pass'.  Measured: that returns a
// nonzero rc inside the runner even though the very same session renders
// Bokeh output through `dash build' moments later, and it made 9 of the 14
// scripts -- every end-to-end one -- skip while the suite reported ALL TESTS
// PASSED.  c(python_exec) is set by Stata's own Python configuration and
// reads without executing anything, so it cannot fail for reasons unrelated
// to Python being present.
if "`c(python_exec)'" == "" {
    display as error "SKIP: Python not available."
    exit 222
}

// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// Locate the repository root and the fixtures.
//
// run_all_cscripts.do cd's into test/ before -do-ing each cscript, which is
// the layout the sibling scripts assume ("../dash.ado").  Being run from the
// repository root is tolerated too.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------
local root ".."
capture confirm file "`root'/dash.ado"
if _rc != 0 {
    local root "."
    capture confirm file "`root'/dash.ado"
    if _rc != 0 {
        display as error "SKIP: cannot locate dash.ado from `c(pwd)'."
        exit 222
    }
}

local corpus  "`root'/test/fixtures/twoway_corpus.do"
local rejjson "`root'/test/fixtures/rejected_options.json"
capture confirm file "`corpus'"
if _rc != 0 {
    local corpus  "`root'/fixtures/twoway_corpus.do"
    local rejjson "`root'/fixtures/rejected_options.json"
}
capture confirm file "`corpus'"
if _rc != 0 {
    display as error "SKIP: corpus fixture twoway_corpus.do not found."
    exit 222
}
capture confirm file "`rejjson'"
if _rc != 0 {
    display as error "SKIP: fixture rejected_options.json not found."
    exit 222
}

do "`root'/dash_parse.mata"
do "`root'/dash.ado"

// A note that names several options is long.  cscript sets linesize 79, which
// would wrap it in the capture log; the scanner below re-joins Stata's "> "
// continuations anyway, but a wide line keeps the diagnostics readable.
capture set linesize 255

local nfail = 0
local faillist ""

// ================================================================
// Helpers
// ================================================================
mata:
mata set matastrict off

// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// _dsp_scan_notes -- read a captured log and locate the contract note.
//
// Stata wraps output at linesize and prefixes the continuation with "> ";
// those are re-joined first, so a note is counted once however it wrapped.
// Sets: dsp_nnotes (count), dsp_note (first note), dsp_notes_all (all, joined
// with " ~~ " so a duplicate-note failure is readable).
// ----------------------------------------------------------------
void _dsp_scan_notes(string scalar fn)
{
    real scalar        fh, i, n, cnt
    string scalar      line, low, joined, first
    string colvector   L

    L = J(0, 1, "")
    fh = fopen(fn, "r")
    while ((line = fget(fh)) != J(0, 0, "")) {
        if (strlen(line) > 0) {
            if (substr(line, strlen(line), 1) == char(13)) {
                line = substr(line, 1, strlen(line) - 1)
            }
        }
        if (substr(line, 1, 2) == "> " & rows(L) > 0) {
            L[rows(L)] = L[rows(L)] + substr(line, 3, .)
        }
        else {
            L = L \ line
        }
    }
    fclose(fh)

    n      = rows(L)
    cnt    = 0
    joined = ""
    first  = ""
    for (i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
        low = strlower(L[i])
        if (strpos(low, "unsupported option") > 0) {
            cnt = cnt + 1
            if (first == "") first = strtrim(L[i])
            if (joined == "") joined = strtrim(L[i])
            else              joined = joined + " ~~ " + strtrim(L[i])
        }
    }
    st_local("dsp_nnotes",    strofreal(cnt))
    st_local("dsp_note",      first)
    st_local("dsp_notes_all", joined)
}

// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// _dsp_names_opt -- does `note' name option `key' as a WHOLE WORD?
// "play" must not be satisfied by "display".
// ----------------------------------------------------------------
real scalar _dsp_names_opt(string scalar note, string scalar key)
{
    string scalar low, k, pat

    low = strlower(note)
    k   = strlower(strtrim(key))
    if (k == "") return(0)
    pat = "(^|[^a-z0-9_])" + k + "([^a-z0-9_]|$)"
    return(regexm(low, pat))
}

// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// _dsp_corpus_counts -- the corpus's probe lines, counted from its text
// without the walk below: every line whose first word is dashprobe or
// dashonlyprobe (dsp_want_probe), and those whose options argument is
// empty and whose plot spec carries no weight (dsp_want_zero).  Read by
// Mata's tokens(), which binds "..." and compound quotes as -args- does,
// and with no program/end state, so the walk's own parsing and skipping
// decide neither number.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------
void _dsp_corpus_counts(string scalar fn)
{
    string colvector L
    string rowvector t
    string scalar    spec, opts
    real scalar      i, np, nz

    L  = cat(fn)
    np = 0
    nz = 0
    for (i = 1; i <= rows(L); i++) {
        t = tokens(L[i])
        if (cols(t) < 1) continue
        if (t[1] != "dashprobe" & t[1] != "dashonlyprobe") continue
        np = np + 1
        spec = ""
        opts = ""
        if (cols(t) >= 3) spec = t[3]
        if (cols(t) >= 4) opts = t[4]
        if (opts == "" & !strpos(spec, "weight=")) nz = nz + 1
    }
    st_local("dsp_want_probe", strofreal(np))
    st_local("dsp_want_zero",  strofreal(nz))
}

end

// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// _dsp_names -- Stata wrapper around _dsp_names_opt.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------
capture program drop _dsp_names
program define _dsp_names, rclass
    args note key
    mata: st_local("dsp_hit", ///
        strofreal(_dsp_names_opt(st_local("note"), st_local("key"))))
    return scalar found = `dsp_hit'
end

// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// _dsp_probe -- run ONE corpus command through dash and capture both its
// return code and the contract note.
//
// The -args- signature is deliberately identical to the corpus harness's
// -dashprobe- (id, spec, opts, twoway_only_extra), so a corpus line can be
// replayed by substituting this program's name for the harness's.  The dash
// command is built exactly as the harness builds it, including the
// "append name(g1) unless the probe supplies its own name()" rule, so the
// command certified here is byte-for-byte the command task 05-01 measured.
//
// twextra is accepted and ignored: it exists only to keep a twoway companion
// option off the dash side.
//
// Returns: r(rc), r(nnotes), r(note), r(cmd).
// ----------------------------------------------------------------
capture program drop _dsp_probe
program define _dsp_probe, rclass
    args id spec opts twextra

    local dcmd `"dash `macval(spec)'"'
    if `"`macval(opts)'"' != "" {
        local dcmd `"`macval(dcmd)', `macval(opts)'"'
        if strpos(`"`macval(opts)'"', "name(") == 0 {
            local dcmd `"`macval(dcmd)' name(g1)"'
        }
    }
    else {
        local dcmd `"`macval(dcmd)', name(g1)"'
    }

    // Clear the registry BEFORE the capture log opens, so "registry cleared."
    // never lands in the window being scanned.
    capture dash clear

    tempfile lg
    capture log close _dsplog
    quietly log using `"`lg'"', replace text name(_dsplog)
    capture noisily `dcmd'
    local rc = _rc
    capture quietly log close _dsplog

    mata: _dsp_scan_notes(st_local("lg"))

    return scalar rc     = `rc'
    return scalar nnotes = `dsp_nnotes'
    return local  note   `"`macval(dsp_note)'"'
    return local  all    `"`macval(dsp_notes_all)'"'
    return local  cmd    `"`macval(dcmd)'"'
end

// ================================================================
// O2-01 / O2-02 -- walk the corpus fixture.
//
// Every -dashprobe- / -dashonlyprobe- line is replayed through _dsp_probe.
// Data-fixture lines are replayed from a whitelist so the t* probes see the
// tsset panel; everything else in the file (program definitions, file
// handles, the version-regression section) is skipped.
// ================================================================
display as text ""
display as text "O2-01/O2-02: replaying the corpus fixture through dash ..."

local nprobe    = 0
local nrcfail   = 0
local nnotefail = 0
local nzeroopt  = 0
local rcfailids ""
local notefailids ""

tempname CF
file open `CF' using "`corpus'", read text
file read `CF' cline
local inprog = 0
while r(eof) == 0 {
    local raw : copy local cline
    gettoken tok rest : raw

    if "`tok'" == "program"                  local inprog = 1
    if "`tok'" == "end" & `inprog' == 1      local inprog = 0

    if `inprog' == 0 {

        // ---- a probe line ----
        if "`tok'" == "dashprobe" | "`tok'" == "dashonlyprobe" {
            local nprobe = `nprobe' + 1
            _dsp_probe `macval(rest)'
            local prc     = r(rc)
            local pnotes  = r(nnotes)
            local pcmd    `"`r(cmd)'"'
            local pall    `"`r(all)'"'

            // the probe id is the first token of the line's arguments
            gettoken pid : rest

            // ---- O2-01: dash must not abort ----
            // Flipped: WP-32 -- mlabwidth(), link() and filter() twoway
            // refuses on every type, r(198), and dash now refuses them as
            // twoway does (BUGS.md "dash names in its note, as not drawn,
            // options twoway refuses on that plot type"); these three
            // dash-only probes are held to twoway's r(198).
            local o2_tw198 0
            if inlist("`pid'", "only_mlabwidth", "only_link", "only_filter") local o2_tw198 1
            if `o2_tw198' & `prc' != 198 {
                local nrcfail = `nrcfail' + 1
                local rcfailids `"`rcfailids' `pid'(`prc')"'
                display as error `"O2-01 FAIL `pid': rc=`prc' from  `macval(pcmd)' (twoway refuses it, r(198))"'
            }
            else if !`o2_tw198' & `prc' != 0 {
                local nrcfail = `nrcfail' + 1
                local rcfailids `"`rcfailids' `pid'(`prc')"'
                display as error `"O2-01 FAIL `pid': rc=`prc' from  `macval(pcmd)'"'
            }

            // ---- O2-02: a zero-option command must emit no note ----
            //
            // A weight expression is not an option, but it IS something
            // dash drops, and since WP-13 the note names it by type
            // (AC-13.1 below).  The corpus control ctl_aweight carries
            // one with no options, so "no options" here means no options
            // and no weight.
            gettoken junk  r2 : rest
            gettoken pspec r3 : r2
            gettoken popts    : r3
            if `"`macval(popts)'"' == "" & strpos(`"`macval(pspec)'"', "weight=") == 0 {
                local nzeroopt = `nzeroopt' + 1
                if `pnotes' != 0 {
                    local nnotefail = `nnotefail' + 1
                    local notefailids `"`notefailids' `pid'"'
                    display as error `"O2-02 FAIL `pid': a command with no options emitted `pnotes' note(s): `macval(pall)'"'
                }
            }
        }

        // ---- a data-fixture line: replay it ----
        //
        // The decision is made from the line's leading TOKENS only.  The whole
        // line is never expanded unless it is about to be executed: the corpus
        // carries commented-out regexes and compound-quoted -file write- lines
        // whose text is not safe to drop into an -if- expression.
        else {
            local doit = 0
            if inlist("`tok'", "sysuse", "use", "webuse", "tsset", "format") ///
                local doit = 1
            if inlist("`tok'", "gen", "generate", "egen", "replace", "sort") ///
                local doit = 1
            if "`tok'" == "clear" {
                gettoken sub : rest
                if "`sub'" == "" local doit = 1       // "clear", never "clear all"
            }
            if "`tok'" == "set" {
                gettoken sub : rest
                if inlist("`sub'", "obs", "seed", "more", "type", "sortseed") ///
                    local doit = 1
            }
            if `doit' == 1 {
                capture quietly `macval(raw)'
                if _rc != 0 {
                    display as error "corpus data line failed (rc=`=_rc'): `macval(raw)'"
                }
            }
        }
    }

    file read `CF' cline
}
file close `CF'

// Both numbers are held to the corpus's own count, not to a floor: O2-01
// asked only for one probe line and O2-02 for none, so a walk that passed
// over probe lines -- or took every command for one with options -- still
// reported every command it saw as passing.  In this corpus a program/end
// state left open swallows all that follows line 68, which the empty-walk
// check does catch; a walk that drops one KIND of probe line (the 18
// dashonlyprobe lines, say) caught nothing.  Measured 24sep2026: 299 probe
// lines (summary.commands_probed in rejected_options.json), 42 of them with
// no option and no weight -- the 43 empty-option lines less ctl_aweight.
mata: _dsp_corpus_counts(st_local("corpus"))

display as text "  corpus commands replayed : `nprobe' (probe lines in the corpus: `dsp_want_probe')"
display as text "  zero-option commands     : `nzeroopt' (in the corpus: `dsp_want_zero')"
display as text "  O2-01 aborts             : `nrcfail'"
display as text "  O2-02 spurious notes     : `nnotefail'"

if `nprobe' == 0 {
    display as error "O2-01 FAIL: the corpus fixture yielded no probe lines."
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist `"`faillist' O2-01(empty-corpus)"'
}
else {
    local o2_bad = 0
    if `nprobe' != `dsp_want_probe' {
        display as error "O2-01 FAIL: the walk replayed `nprobe' commands;" ///
            " the corpus holds `dsp_want_probe' probe lines."
        local nfail = `nfail' + 1
        local faillist `"`faillist' O2-01(count)"'
        local o2_bad = 1
    }
    if `nrcfail' != 0 {
        display as error "O2-01 FAIL: `nrcfail' of `nprobe' corpus commands abort;" ///
            " dash.sthlp:668-673 promises none do."
        display as error "  failing:`rcfailids'"
        local nfail = `nfail' + 1
        local faillist `"`faillist' O2-01"'
        local o2_bad = 1
    }
    if `o2_bad' == 0 {
        display as text "O2-01 PASS: all `nprobe' corpus commands return rc=0"
    }
}

if `nprobe' > 0 {
    local o2_bad = 0
    if `dsp_want_zero' == 0 | `nzeroopt' != `dsp_want_zero' {
        display as error "O2-02 FAIL: the walk took `nzeroopt' commands for ones with no" ///
            " option and no weight; the corpus holds `dsp_want_zero', and must hold some."
        local nfail = `nfail' + 1
        local faillist `"`faillist' O2-02(count)"'
        local o2_bad = 1
    }
    if `nnotefail' != 0 {
        display as error "O2-02 FAIL: `nnotefail' command(s) with no options emitted a note."
        display as error "  failing:`notefailids'"
        local nfail = `nfail' + 1
        local faillist `"`faillist' O2-02"'
        local o2_bad = 1
    }
    if `o2_bad' == 0 {
        display as text "O2-02 PASS: all `nzeroopt' zero-option commands emit no note"
    }
}

// ================================================================
// O2-03 -- the "accept-and-report" options, read from the fixture.
//
// Each must be accepted AND reported.  dash.sthlp:157-160 already promises a
// warning for play() and nodraw.
// ================================================================
qui sysuse auto, clear

// The dispositions are read by Python's JSON parser, as the other scripts
// read their JSON fixtures (test_abbreviations.cscript).  A line regex read
// them, relying on the file's pretty printing and on each entry's keys
// running option ... disposition ... dash_command: an entry written in
// another order, or on fewer lines, was passed over without a word, and
// O2-03 had only to find one.  The number read must be the fixture's own
// tally, summary.by_disposition's "accept-and-report" -- 3 on 24sep2026:
// play, xoverhangs and yoverhangs.  Each entry's option and the
// dash_command of its first probe come back as DSP_AR_OPT_# and
// DSP_AR_CMD_#, copied into locals through Mata so that nothing in them is
// expanded.
global DSP_REJJSON "`rejjson'"
python:
import json as _dsp_json
from sfi import Macro as _dsp_M
with open(_dsp_M.getGlobal("DSP_REJJSON"), encoding="utf-8") as _dsp_fh:
    _dsp_d = _dsp_json.load(_dsp_fh)
_dsp_ar = [o for o in _dsp_d.get("rejected_options", [])
           if isinstance(o, dict) and o.get("disposition") == "accept-and-report"]
_dsp_M.setGlobal("DSP_AR_N", str(len(_dsp_ar)))
for _dsp_i, _dsp_o in enumerate(_dsp_ar, 1):
    _dsp_p = _dsp_o.get("probes") or [{}]
    _dsp_M.setGlobal("DSP_AR_OPT_" + str(_dsp_i), str(_dsp_o.get("option", "")))
    _dsp_M.setGlobal("DSP_AR_CMD_" + str(_dsp_i), str(_dsp_p[0].get("dash_command", "")))
_dsp_M.setGlobal("DSP_AR_WANT", str(_dsp_d.get("summary", {}).get("by_disposition", {}).get("accept-and-report", "")))
end
local dsp_ar_n = ${DSP_AR_N}
local dsp_ar_want "${DSP_AR_WANT}"
forvalues i = 1/`dsp_ar_n' {
    mata: st_local("dsp_ar_opt_`i'", st_global("DSP_AR_OPT_`i'"))
    mata: st_local("dsp_ar_cmd_`i'", st_global("DSP_AR_CMD_`i'"))
}
macro drop DSP_*

display as text ""
display as text "O2-03: accept-and-report options from rejected_options.json (`dsp_ar_n' found; the fixture's tally: `dsp_ar_want')"

local ar_count_bad = 0
if `dsp_ar_n' == 0 {
    display as error "O2-03 FAIL: no accept-and-report dispositions found in the fixture."
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist `"`faillist' O2-03(no-fixture-rows)"'
}
else if "`dsp_ar_n'" != "`dsp_ar_want'" {
    display as error "O2-03 FAIL: `dsp_ar_n' accept-and-report entries were read;" ///
        " the fixture's summary counts `dsp_ar_want'."
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist `"`faillist' O2-03(count)"'
    local ar_count_bad = 1
}

local ar_optlist ""
local ar_keylist ""
local n_ar_fail = 0

forvalues i = 1/`dsp_ar_n' {
    local key : copy local dsp_ar_opt_`i'
    local cmd : copy local dsp_ar_cmd_`i'

    // "dash <spec>, <opts> name(g1)"  ->  spec / opts, with name(g1) removed
    local body  = substr(`"`macval(cmd)'"', 6, .)
    local cpos  = strpos(`"`macval(body)'"', ",")
    // An entry that cannot be probed fails: it used to be skipped and left
    // out of the tally, and the summary still said "all accepted and
    // reported" of a set it had not probed.
    if `cpos' == 0 {
        display as error `"O2-03 FAIL `key': the fixture's dash_command has no option list to probe: `macval(cmd)'"'
        local n_ar_fail = `n_ar_fail' + 1
        continue
    }
    local spec  = substr(`"`macval(body)'"', 1, `cpos' - 1)
    local opts  = trim(substr(`"`macval(body)'"', `cpos' + 1, .))
    local opts  = trim(subinstr(`"`macval(opts)'"', "name(g1)", "", 1))

    local ar_optlist `"`macval(ar_optlist)' `macval(opts)'"'
    // Flipped (WP-31 D5): the drawn overhangs are given in O2-04's one
    // command but are not among the names its note must hold.
    if !inlist("`key'", "xoverhangs", "yoverhangs") {
        local ar_keylist `"`ar_keylist' `key'"'
    }

    _dsp_probe "ar_`key'" `"`macval(spec)'"' `"`macval(opts)'"'
    local prc    = r(rc)
    local pnotes = r(nnotes)
    local pnote  `"`r(note)'"'
    local pcmd   `"`r(cmd)'"'

    local bad = 0
    // Flipped (WP-31 D5): xoverhangs and yoverhangs named in the note was
    // wrong once dash drew them (sizing_truth.json overhang_x1): accepted,
    // and named by nothing.
    local honoured = inlist("`key'", "xoverhangs", "yoverhangs")
    if `prc' != 0 {
        display as error `"O2-03 FAIL `key': rc=`prc' from  `macval(pcmd)'"'
        local bad = 1
    }
    else if `honoured' {
        if `pnotes' != 0 {
            display as error `"O2-03 FAIL `key': drawn, yet named: `macval(pnote)'"'
            local bad = 1
        }
    }
    else if `pnotes' != 1 {
        display as error `"O2-03 FAIL `key': expected exactly 1 note, got `pnotes'."'
        local bad = 1
    }
    else {
        _dsp_names `"`macval(pnote)'"' "`key'"
        if r(found) == 0 {
            display as error `"O2-03 FAIL `key': the note does not name it: `macval(pnote)'"'
            local bad = 1
        }
    }
    if `bad' == 1 local n_ar_fail = `n_ar_fail' + 1
    else display as text "  O2-03 ok: `key' accepted and reported"
}

if `dsp_ar_n' > 0 {
    if `n_ar_fail' != 0 {
        display as error "O2-03 FAIL: `n_ar_fail' of `dsp_ar_n' accept-and-report options" ///
            " are not accepted-and-reported."
        local nfail = `nfail' + 1
        local faillist `"`faillist' O2-03"'
    }
    else if `ar_count_bad' == 0 {
        display as text "O2-03 PASS: all `dsp_ar_n' accept-and-report options accepted and reported"
    }
}

// ================================================================
// O2-04 -- several unsupported options in ONE command produce exactly ONE
// note, that names ALL of them and does NOT name the supported option used
// alongside them.
// ================================================================
display as text ""
if `dsp_ar_n' > 0 {
    local combo `"mcolor(red)`macval(ar_optlist)'"'
    _dsp_probe "combo" "scatter mpg weight" `"`macval(combo)'"'
    local prc    = r(rc)
    local pnotes = r(nnotes)
    local pnote  `"`r(note)'"'
    local pall   `"`r(all)'"'
    local pcmd   `"`r(cmd)'"'

    local bad = 0
    if `prc' != 0 {
        display as error `"O2-04 FAIL: rc=`prc' from  `macval(pcmd)'"'
        local bad = 1
    }
    else if `pnotes' != 1 {
        display as error `"O2-04 FAIL: expected exactly 1 note for `dsp_ar_n' unsupported options, got `pnotes': `macval(pall)'"'
        local bad = 1
    }
    else {
        foreach key of local ar_keylist {
            _dsp_names `"`macval(pnote)'"' "`key'"
            if r(found) == 0 {
                display as error `"O2-04 FAIL: the one note omits `key': `macval(pnote)'"'
                local bad = 1
            }
        }
        // the supported option must NOT be reported as dropped
        _dsp_names `"`macval(pnote)'"' "mcolor"
        if r(found) == 1 {
            display as error `"O2-04 FAIL: the note names the SUPPORTED option mcolor(): `macval(pnote)'"'
            local bad = 1
        }
    }

    if `bad' == 1 {
        local nfail = `nfail' + 1
        local faillist `"`faillist' O2-04"'
    }
    else {
        display as text "O2-04 PASS: `dsp_ar_n' unsupported options -> one note naming all of them"
    }
}

// ================================================================
// O2-05 -- an option twoway takes and dash does not draw is accepted and
// reported.  Flipped: WP-32 -- the option was one twoway refuses, r(198), which dash
// now refuses as twoway does (BUGS.md "In a few mixed lists dash names
// another word than twoway names first, and an unknown lower-case word is
// noted where twoway refuses it"); afcolor() twoway takes on every type.
// ================================================================
display as text ""
_dsp_probe "unknown" "scatter mpg weight" "afcolor(red)"
local prc    = r(rc)
local pnotes = r(nnotes)
local pnote  `"`r(note)'"'
local pcmd   `"`r(cmd)'"'

local bad = 0
if `prc' != 0 {
    display as error `"O2-05 FAIL: rc=`prc' from  `macval(pcmd)'"'
    local bad = 1
}
else if `pnotes' != 1 {
    display as error `"O2-05 FAIL: expected exactly 1 note, got `pnotes'."'
    local bad = 1
}
else {
    _dsp_names `"`macval(pnote)'"' "afcolor"
    if r(found) == 0 {
        display as error `"O2-05 FAIL: the note does not name afcolor(): `macval(pnote)'"'
        local bad = 1
    }
}
if `bad' == 1 {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist `"`faillist' O2-05"'
}
else display as text "O2-05 PASS: an option dash does not draw is accepted and reported"

// ================================================================
// O2-06 -- unsupported options in TWO different plot segments are BOTH
// reported, in the single per-command note.  Flipped: WP-32 -- the option was one twoway refuses, r(198), which dash
// now refuses as twoway does (BUGS.md "In a few mixed lists dash names
// another word than twoway names first, and an unknown lower-case word is
// noted where twoway refuses it"); afcolor() and
// afintensity() twoway takes on every type.
// ================================================================
display as text ""
_dsp_probe "twoseg" "scatter mpg weight, afcolor(red) || line mpg weight" ///
    "afintensity(50)"
local prc    = r(rc)
local pnotes = r(nnotes)
local pnote  `"`r(note)'"'
local pall   `"`r(all)'"'
local pcmd   `"`r(cmd)'"'

local bad = 0
if `prc' != 0 {
    display as error `"O2-06 FAIL: rc=`prc' from  `macval(pcmd)'"'
    local bad = 1
}
else if `pnotes' != 1 {
    display as error `"O2-06 FAIL: expected exactly 1 note across the two segments, got `pnotes': `macval(pall)'"'
    local bad = 1
}
else {
    foreach key in afcolor afintensity {
        _dsp_names `"`macval(pnote)'"' "`key'"
        if r(found) == 0 {
            display as error `"O2-06 FAIL: the note omits segment option `key': `macval(pnote)'"'
            local bad = 1
        }
    }
}
if `bad' == 1 {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist `"`faillist' O2-06"'
}
else display as text "O2-06 PASS: both segments' unsupported options are in the one note"

// ================================================================
// O2-07 -- a command whose options are ALL supported emits NO note.
// The guard against a fix that simply reports everything.
// ================================================================
display as text ""
_dsp_probe "supported" "scatter mpg weight" `"mcolor(red) msize(small) title("T")"'
local prc    = r(rc)
local pnotes = r(nnotes)
local pall   `"`r(all)'"'
local pcmd   `"`r(cmd)'"'

local bad = 0
if `prc' != 0 {
    display as error `"O2-07 FAIL: rc=`prc' from  `macval(pcmd)'"'
    local bad = 1
}
else if `pnotes' != 0 {
    display as error `"O2-07 FAIL: a fully supported command emitted `pnotes' note(s): `macval(pall)'"'
    local bad = 1
}
if `bad' == 1 {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist `"`faillist' O2-07"'
}
else display as text "O2-07 PASS: a fully supported command emits no note"

// ================================================================
// O2-08 -- link() and filter() written on a graph are refused, as twoway
// refuses them.
//
// ROADMAP WP-13 TR-13.1 / GAPS.md E2.  Both belong to dash build; written
// on a graph they were stored in graph_options and read by nothing, and
// the note did not name them (measured 22sep2026: rc 0, no note); WP-13
// named them.  Flipped: WP-32 -- twoway refuses both on every type and
// after the plot groups' comma, "option link() not allowed", r(198)
// (test/fixtures/noted_option_truth.json), and dash now refuses them as
// twoway does, naming the first; the note names nothing.
// ================================================================
display as text ""
_dsp_probe "gl_link_filter" "scatter mpg weight" `"mcolor(red) link(g1) filter(foreign, type(dropdown))"'
local prc    = r(rc)
local pnotes = r(nnotes)
local pcmd   `"`r(cmd)'"'
local bad = 0
if `prc' != 198 {
    display as error `"O2-08 FAIL: rc=`prc' from  `macval(pcmd)' (twoway: r(198))"'
    local bad = 1
}
else if `pnotes' != 0 {
    display as error `"O2-08 FAIL: expected no note, got `pnotes'"'
    local bad = 1
}
if `bad' == 1 {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist `"`faillist' O2-08"'
}
else display as text "O2-08 PASS: link() and filter() written on a graph are refused, r(198), as twoway refuses them"

// ================================================================
// O2-09 -- saving() on a NAMED graph is named, once, and writes nothing.
// A named graph is written by `dash build, saving()'; measured 22sep2026:
// name(g3) saving(x.html) registered g3, wrote nothing and said nothing.
// ================================================================
local o2_named "`c(tmpdir)'o2_named_saving.html"
capture erase "`o2_named'"
_dsp_probe "named_saving" "scatter mpg weight" `"saving("`o2_named'")"'
local prc    = r(rc)
local pnotes = r(nnotes)
local pnote  `"`r(note)'"'
local pcmd   `"`r(cmd)'"'
local bad = 0
if `prc' != 0 {
    display as error `"O2-09 FAIL: rc=`prc' from  `macval(pcmd)'"'
    local bad = 1
}
else if `pnotes' != 1 {
    display as error `"O2-09 FAIL: expected exactly 1 note, got `pnotes'"'
    local bad = 1
}
else {
    _dsp_names `"`macval(pnote)'"' "saving"
    if r(found) != 1 {
        display as error `"O2-09 FAIL: the note does not name saving(): `macval(pnote)'"'
        local bad = 1
    }
    local once = subinstr(`"`macval(pnote)'"', "saving()", "", 1)
    _dsp_names `"`macval(once)'"' "saving"
    if r(found) != 0 {
        display as error `"O2-09 FAIL: saving() is named more than once: `macval(pnote)'"'
        local bad = 1
    }
}
capture confirm file "`o2_named'"
if _rc == 0 {
    display as error "O2-09 FAIL: saving() on a named graph wrote a file"
    capture erase "`o2_named'"
    local bad = 1
}
if `bad' == 1 {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist `"`faillist' O2-09"'
}
else display as text "O2-09 PASS: saving() on a named graph is named once and writes nothing"

// ================================================================
// O2-10 -- the immediate route still honours saving() and is not told
// otherwise: the guard against reporting saving() from a static list.
// ================================================================
if `"`c(python_exec)'"' != "" {
    local o2_imm "`c(tmpdir)'o2_imm_saving.html"
    capture erase "`o2_imm'"
    tempfile immlg
    capture log close _dspimm
    quietly log using `"`immlg'"', replace text name(_dspimm)
    capture noisily dash scatter mpg weight, saving("`o2_imm'")
    local prc = _rc
    capture quietly log close _dspimm
    mata: _dsp_scan_notes(st_local("immlg"))
    local bad = 0
    if `prc' != 0 {
        display as error "O2-10 FAIL: rc=`prc' from an immediate render with saving()"
        local bad = 1
    }
    if `dsp_nnotes' != 0 {
        display as error `"O2-10 FAIL: the immediate render emitted a note: `macval(dsp_notes_all)'"'
        local bad = 1
    }
    capture confirm file "`o2_imm'"
    if _rc != 0 {
        display as error "O2-10 FAIL: the immediate render did not write its file"
        local bad = 1
    }
    capture erase "`o2_imm'"
    if `bad' == 1 {
        local nfail = `nfail' + 1
        local faillist `"`faillist' O2-10"'
    }
    else display as text "O2-10 PASS: the immediate render honours saving() with no note"
}
else display as text "O2-10 SKIP: the immediate render needs Python"

// ================================================================
// AC-13.1 -- a weight on a glyph layer is accepted and never named.
//
// ROADMAP WP-13 TR-13.2 / GAPS.md A3 made the note name the TYPE, never
// the variable.  Flipped (WP-31 C9): twoway sizes markers by the weight and
// says nothing (weighted_markers_truth.json W01); on markerless types
// twoway is silent too (W07) -- so dash draws the weight on the marker
// types and names it nowhere.
// ================================================================
display as text ""
foreach case in "scatter mpg weight [aw=price]" ///
                "(scatter mpg weight [aw=price]) (line mpg weight)" ///
                "(scatter mpg weight [aw=price]) (line mpg weight [aw=price])" ///
                "(lfit mpg weight [aw=price]) (scatter mpg weight [fw=rep78])" {
    _dsp_probe "weight" `"`case'"' ""
    local prc    = r(rc)
    local pnotes = r(nnotes)
    local pnote  `"`r(note)'"'
    local bad = 0
    if `prc' != 0 | `pnotes' != 0 {
        display as error `"AC-13.1 FAIL: rc=`prc' notes=`pnotes' (`macval(pnote)') for  `case'"'
        local bad = 1
    }
    if `bad' == 1 {
        local nfail = `nfail' + 1
        local faillist `"`faillist' AC-13.1"'
    }
    else display as text `"AC-13.1 PASS: rc 0 and no note for  `case'"'
}

// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// Summary
// ----------------------------------------------------------------
capture dash clear
display as text ""
display as text "============================================================"
if `nfail' == 0 {
    display as text "  test_option_surface: ALL CHECKS PASSED"
    display as text "============================================================"
}
else {
    display as error "  test_option_surface: `nfail' CHECK(S) FAILED"
    display as error "  failing:`faillist'"
    display as text "============================================================"
    exit 9
}
